{#
  The addresses this host accepts mail for, and the only thing that
  lets Postfix answer "does this recipient exist" during the SMTP
  transaction.

  It was empty until 2026-08-17 while virtual_mailbox_domains named
  both domains, so Postfix answered `250 2.1.5 Ok` to every address in
  either one, handed it to Dovecot over LMTP, was refused there, and
  generated a bounce afterwards. On spam the envelope sender is
  forged, so the bounce went to a third party - backscatter this host
  emitted rather than received, and the source of both DMARC `reject`
  records that arrived on 2026-08-17.

  Two sources, unioned:

    - every account roles/users manages, crossed with every domain
      this host serves. Delivery is by LMTP to Dovecot, whose
      `auth_username_format = %n` strips the domain before the userdb
      lookup, so <user>@<any served domain> resolves to the same
      system account and the same Maildir. That is why this is a cross
      product and not a per-domain list.

    - every alias in mail.aliases, on every domain, matching exactly
      what valiases.j2 generates.

  The aliases are redundant as far as Postfix is concerned: it
  consults virtual_alias_maps before this map when deciding whether a
  recipient exists, so an aliased address is accepted either way. They
  are listed anyway so that this one file answers "which addresses
  does this host accept" - the same reasoning that makes
  virtual_alias_domains explicitly empty in main.cf. Listing them
  changes nothing about where the mail goes: alias expansion still
  runs first, in cleanup, so an address with an alias entry is
  rewritten and never delivered to a mailbox of its own.

  The right-hand side is ignored. virtual_transport is LMTP, so
  Postfix only ever asks whether the key exists; `OK` is the
  convention for saying so.

  What is deliberately NOT here: $myhostname and localhost. Those are
  in mydestination, a different address class, validated against
  local_recipient_maps instead - which is left at its default of the
  system passwd file plus /etc/aliases. Mail to root@mail.<domain> is
  unaffected by this file.
#}
# Valid recipients for Postfix's virtual mailbox domains
{% set addresses = [] %}
{% for d in [domain] + domain_aliases %}
{%   for account in users.users %}
{%     set _ = addresses.append(account.name ~ '@' ~ d) %}
{%   endfor %}
{%   for entry in mail.aliases %}
{%     set _ = addresses.append(entry.alias ~ '@' ~ d) %}
{%   endfor %}
{% endfor %}
{% for address in addresses | unique %}
{{ address }} OK
{% endfor %}
